usage: NGSpeciesID [-h] [--version] [--debug]
                   (--fastq FASTQ | --use_old_sorted_file) [--t NR_CORES]
                   [--d PRINT_OUTPUT] [--q QUALITY_THRESHOLD] [--ont]
                   [--isoseq] [--consensus]
                   [--abundance_ratio ABUNDANCE_RATIO]
                   [--rc_identity_threshold RC_IDENTITY_THRESHOLD]
                   [--max_seqs_for_consensus MAX_SEQS_FOR_CONSENSUS]
                   [--medaka | --racon] [--medaka_model MEDAKA_MODEL]
                   [--medaka_fastq] [--racon_iter RACON_ITER]
                   [--remove_universal_tails | --primer_file PRIMER_FILE]
                   [--primer_max_ed PRIMER_MAX_ED] [--trim_window TRIM_WINDOW]
                   [--m TARGET_LENGTH] [--s TARGET_DEVIATION]
                   [--sample_size SAMPLE_SIZE] [--top_reads] [--k K] [--w W]
                   [--min_shared MIN_SHARED]
                   [--mapped_threshold MAPPED_THRESHOLD]
                   [--aligned_threshold ALIGNED_THRESHOLD]
                   [--symmetric_map_align_thresholds]
                   [--batch_type BATCH_TYPE] [--min_fraction MIN_FRACTION]
                   [--min_prob_no_hits MIN_PROB_NO_HITS]
                   [--outfolder OUTFOLDER]
                   {write_fastq} ...

Reference-free clustering and consensus forming of targeted ONT or PacBio
reads

positional arguments:
  {write_fastq}         sub-command help
    write_fastq         a help

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
  --debug               Enable debug logging (default: False)
  --fastq FASTQ         Path to consensus fastq file(s) (default: None)
  --use_old_sorted_file
                        Using already existing sorted file if present in
                        specified output directory. (default: False)
  --t NR_CORES          Number of cores allocated for clustering (default: 8)
  --d PRINT_OUTPUT      For debugging, prints status of clustering and
                        minimizer database every p reads processed. (default:
                        10000)
  --q QUALITY_THRESHOLD
                        Filters reads with average phred quality value under
                        this number (default = 7.0). (default: 7.0)
  --ont                 Clustering of ONT transcript reads. (default: False)
  --isoseq              Clustering of PacBio Iso-Seq reads. (default: False)
  --consensus           After clustering, (1) run spoa on all clusters, (2)
                        detect reverse complements, (3) run medaka. (default:
                        False)
  --abundance_ratio ABUNDANCE_RATIO
                        Threshold for --consensus algorithm. Consider only
                        clusters larger than a fraction of number of total
                        reads (default 0.1) (default: 0.1)
  --rc_identity_threshold RC_IDENTITY_THRESHOLD
                        Threshold for --consensus algorithm. Define a reverse
                        complement if identity is over this threshold (default
                        0.9) (default: 0.9)
  --max_seqs_for_consensus MAX_SEQS_FOR_CONSENSUS
                        Maximum number of seqs to form consensus with spoa
                        [INT] (default = -1, which means to use all sequences
                        available regardless of cluster size). (default: -1)
  --medaka              Run final medaka polishing algorithm. (default: False)
  --racon               Run final racon polishing algorithm. (default: False)
  --medaka_model MEDAKA_MODEL
                        Set specific medaka model. (default: )
  --medaka_fastq        Request Medaka to output a FASTQ file, instead of
                        FASTA (default: False)
  --racon_iter RACON_ITER
                        Number of times to run racon iteratively (default: 2)
  --remove_universal_tails
                        Remove universal tails "TTTCTGTTGGTGCTGATATTGC" and
                        "ACTTGCCTGTCGCTCTATCTTC" after the spoa consensus step
                        and before the revers complement detection. (default:
                        False)
  --primer_file PRIMER_FILE
                        Path to file with primers. Primers are removed after
                        the spoa consensus step and before the revers
                        complement detection. (default: )
  --primer_max_ed PRIMER_MAX_ED
                        Threshold edit distance for finding bracore in spoa
                        consensus (default: 2)
  --trim_window TRIM_WINDOW
                        Window size of how many bases to look for barcodes
                        (default 150 bases in beginning and end of consensus).
                        (default: 150)
  --m TARGET_LENGTH     Intended amplicon length. Invoked to filter out reads
                        with length greater than m + s or smaller than m - s
                        (default = 0 which means no filtering) (default: 0)
  --s TARGET_DEVIATION  Maximum allowed amplicon-length deviation. Invoked to
                        filter out reads with length greater than m + s or
                        smaller than m - s (default = 0 which means no
                        filtering) (default: 0)
  --sample_size SAMPLE_SIZE
                        Use sample_size reads in the NGSpecies pipeline
                        (default = 0 which means all reads considered). If
                        sample size is larger than actual number of reads, all
                        reads will be used. (default: 0)
  --top_reads           Use the top --sample_size reads instead of a random
                        selection (default = false, which means random reads
                        considered). (default: False)
  --k K                 Kmer size (default: 13)
  --w W                 Window size (default: 20)
  --min_shared MIN_SHARED
                        Minmum number of minimizers shared between read and
                        cluster (default: 5)
  --mapped_threshold MAPPED_THRESHOLD
                        Minmum mapped fraction of read to be included in
                        cluster. The density of minimizers to classify a
                        region as mapped depends on quality of the read.
                        (default: 0.7)
  --aligned_threshold ALIGNED_THRESHOLD
                        Minmum aligned fraction of read to be included in
                        cluster. Aligned identity depends on the quality of
                        the read. (default: 0.4)
  --symmetric_map_align_thresholds
                        Apply mapped threshold and aligned threshold to
                        fraction of cluster representative which maps onto the
                        read (default: False)
  --batch_type BATCH_TYPE
                        In parrallel mode, how to split the reads into chunks
                        "total_nt", "nr_reads", or "weighted" (default:
                        total_nt) (default: total_nt)
  --min_fraction MIN_FRACTION
                        Minmum fraction of minimizers shared compared to best
                        hit, in order to continue mapping. (default: 0.8)
  --min_prob_no_hits MIN_PROB_NO_HITS
                        Minimum probability for i consecutive minimizers to be
                        different between read and representative and still
                        considered as mapped region, under assumption that
                        they come from the same transcript (depends on read
                        quality). (default: 0.1)
  --outfolder OUTFOLDER
                        A fasta file with transcripts that are shared between
                        samples and have perfect illumina support. (default:
                        None)
